"35669","Banana Coconut treat","I love bananas and I love the coconut it is a perfect combination.","5.0","2.0","5","1","2 bananas | 2 cups    coconut | 1 orange","Take the bananas and peel them. | (cut off the ends if you would like to.). | Take the orange and squeeze it over the 2 bananas. | (this will make the coconut stick.) Roll it in the coconut and serve.","","Lunch"
"35677","Sweet & Hot Mustard","This is so good on ham. I like it on egg sandwiches too. Use it in a variety of ways. Good on hard salami too.","0.0","","12","0","1⁄2 cup    mustard powder | 2⁄3 cup    white vinegar | 2⁄3 cup    granulated sugar | 1 egg","Put all ingredients in a food processor bowl and process till smooth. | Using a double boiler pan, put water in pan and bring to a boil. | Pour mustard mixture in top of pan. | Reduce heat to low and cook mixture, stirring constantly with a wire whip, for about 7 minutes or till mixture is smooth and thickened. | Store in pint jelly jar or airtight container in refrigerator.","","Sauces"
"35685","Ayran - Chilled Turkish Yoghurt Drink","A very refreshing, tasty and healthy Turkish drink, that not only kids will like.","3.5","","10","3","1 1⁄4 cups    plain yogurt | 2 cups    carbonated water (Perrier plain) | 1⁄2 teaspoon    salt | 1 tablespoon    fresh lemon juice | 1 1⁄2 teaspoons    ground cumin","Mix well all ingredients in a blender. | Taste, you may want to increase the salt or lemon juice. | Chill. | Serve cool, like a beverage.","","Beverages"
"35686","Vanilla Ice Cream","If you like ""snowcream"" you will love this! This recipe came from our church cookbook. My husband and I think this is the next best thing to ""snowcream"". I use a 1 1/2 quart freezer. I usually get about 2 freezers out of this. I just store in the refridgerator till ready to use.
